            <ArticleTitle>Humanized Anti-IL-5 Antibody Therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>509</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cell.2016.04.020</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0092-8674(16)30411-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eosinophils are suppressed by a new class of drugs targeting Interleukin-5 (IL-5), an eosinophil growth, activation, and survival factor. Humanized anti-IL-5 antibodies are effective in treating asthma patients with the severe eosinophilic form of the disease and are the first new class of asthma drugs approved in 12 years.</AbstractText>
